==Rarity==
Cat Units are sorted into six different '''rarities''': [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]], [[:Category:Special Cats|Special]], [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]], [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare]], [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Super Rare]] and [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]]. Rarer cats tend to be more powerful, but also cost more to deploy and recharge slower. Several subgroups exist within these rarities, with a few examples being [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] (Special), [[:Category:Li'l Cats|Li'l Cats]] (Special) and [[:Category:Crazed Cats|Crazed Cats]] (Super Rare).

==Forms==
Every Cat Unit has up to four different '''forms''' that they can switch to and from between battles: '''Normal''', '''Evolved''', '''[[True Form|True]] and [[Ultra Form|Ultra]]'''. Each form has a different name, appearance and potentially stats and abilities.

When unlocked, each unit only has access to its Normal Form. The Evolved Form is automatically unlocked upon reaching level 10 and will usually have higher health and attack power or no stat changes at all. True Forms, however, tend to have different requirements depending on the unit:
*[[:Category:Gacha Cats|Gacha Cats]]' True Forms can be unlocked using a set amount of [[Catfruit]] and XP when at level 30 or above;
*[[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]]' True Forms are automatically unlocked at level 20+10 (except [[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|Superfeline]], which evolves at 20+80);
*Other non-gacha cats typically require the player to beat their [[:Category:Awakening Stages|Awakening Stages]] and upgrade them to level 20.
True Forms provide different bonuses depending on the unit but are usually more powerful than either of the previous forms. For some Cat Units such as the [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]] units, different forms can have entirely different roles.

